SUMMARY:What Enterprise AI Looks Like When It Works
DESCRIPTION:All Things AI (Live)\nIn this session of *Newsweek’s* “AI 
 Impact Forum\,” **Dr. Ranjit Tinaikar** sits down with **Firdaus Bhathen
 a**\, executive vice president and chief technology and transformation off
 icer at S&P Global\, to examine what it takes to turn advances in AI into 
 meaningful business impact.\nDrawing on Bhathena's experience leading tech
 nology and transformation at S&P Global and previously at FIS Global and C
 VS Health\, the conversation will explore why trusted\, differentiated dat
 a becomes increasingly important as powerful AI models become more widely 
 available—and what companies need to do to put that data to work.\nBhath
 ena and Tinaikar will discuss moving beyond experimentation\, making data 
 governed and reusable\, redesigning workflows around new capabilities and 
 balancing speed with trust\, security and resilience. They will also exami
 ne how leaders can keep technology initiatives focused on customer problem
 s and identify where genuine competitive advantage can emerge.\n\nDesigned
  for CEOs\, CIOs\, CTOs\, transformation leaders and senior technology dec
 ision-makers\, the session will offer a practical look at the choices orga
 nizations face as they move AI deeper into their operations and pursue mea
 surable business impact.\n\nRegister here: https://app.sequel.io/newsweek/
 firdaus-bhathena-sp-global-enterprise-ai
