SUMMARY:The AI Election: How Artificial Intelligence Shaped the 2026 Midte
 rms
DESCRIPTION:All Things AI (Live)\nOne week after Election Day\, *Newsweek*
  will bring together policy experts and Washington insiders to examine the
  2026 midterm results through the lens of artificial intelligence.\n\nThe 
 discussion will draw on *Newsweek’s* **[AI Policy Scorecard](https://www
 .newsweek.com/ai-policy-scorecard)**\, which tracks the public records of 
 all 537 sitting members of Congress across five areas of AI policy: regula
 tion and governance\, data centers and energy\, jobs and the economy\, saf
 ety and privacy\, and national security and China.\nUsing those findings a
 s a starting point\, the panel will look at what the results reveal about 
 the emerging politics of AI: where the issue mattered\, how positions cut 
 across traditional party lines\, and how the composition of the next Congr
 ess could reshape the policy fights ahead.\n\nThe panel will feature **Nat
 haniel Persily**\, James B. McClatchy professor of law at Stanford Law Sch
 ool and co-director of the Stanford Law AI Initiative and the Stanford AI 
 Governance Lab\; **Brent Buchanan**\, founder and CEO of Cygnal\; **Nick P
 enniman**\, founder and CEO of Issue One\; and **Andrew Mamo**\, communica
 tions advisor at The Bench.\n\nModerated by **Gabriel Snyder**\, *Newsweek
 ’s* executive editor\, enterprise\, the conversation will also explore h
 ow campaigns and outside groups approached AI during the election\, what t
 he results mean for lobbying and advocacy in Washington and which question
 s are likely to confront lawmakers.\n\nRegister here: https://app.sequel.i
 o/newsweek/ai-policy-midterms
